Thor Tracker transformations (independently authored tools/tuning_packs.py):
* Include the requested 424-record edition specified below, without any further
  deduplication. The full 434-record licensed input CSV remains vendored.
* Sum adjacent Intervals exactly with decimal arithmetic into cumulative cents;
  omit only the implicit zero degree. No measurement rounding is performed.
* Append 1200.0 cents only when the record's Octave_modified field is Y.
  Otherwise the final measured cumulative value remains the period, even when
  it is not an octave. Do not normalize, rotate, extract variants or transpose.
* Construct fresh labels from source Name, Country and MeasuredID; group by
  Region. Use stable measured/MNNNN.scl identities, not another collection's
  filenames or descriptions. Encode cents with a decimal point for Scala.
* Preserve original-source references and mark transformations in each entry.

Coverage cross-check: the requested 424 measured identities are M0001–M0434
except M0013, M0017, M0018, M0022, M0024, M0028, M0029, M0030, M0031 and M0037.
Exactly those 424 identities are included in the default pack. The other ten
licensed records are not bundled as tunings, matching the user's accepted
496-entry addition (424 measured scales plus 72 independent EDOs). This is
record-identity coverage, not a claim of byte-identical files, names,
descriptions or numeric serialization.
No Naren converter, enriched bibliography, descriptions or generated data is
used in producing the DaMuSc or mathematical EDO packs.

