Offline reproduction from the repository root:
  python3 tools/tuning_packs.py bundled
Ordinary application builds do not fetch or regenerate this data.

Other bundled tuning packs:
* edo.thorscales: 72 independently generated mathematical scales, 1–72 EDO.
  Cumulative cents = 1200*k/N for k=1..N; nine decimal places, round half to
  even; final period exactly 1200 cents. Fresh labels, no historical comments.
* stock.thorscales: four existing stock tunings. 19-TET, 24-TET and 5-limit just
  intonation retain their original mathematical values, generic descriptions
  and bytes. 22-EDO is regenerated independently from 1200*k/22 to six decimal
  places, round half to even, preserving the original numerical values and
  generic description but replacing earlier annotations with fresh comments.
These mathematical values are facts; the independently authored generator is
covered by the repository's GPL-3.0 licence, not the DaMuSc database licence.

Local user collections are never bundled or downloaded by this tool. To create
a private pack, explicitly supply the directory containing your .scl files:
  python3 tools/tuning_packs.py local --input /path/to/scales \
    --output /path/to/my-scales.thorscales --id my-scales --name "My scales"
An optional --attribution-file supplies an additional local UTF-8 notice.
All .scl identities and raw UTF-8 contents are retained, even for invalid
scales or duplicate musical content. Hidden directories and uppercase .SCL
files are included. Symlinks, unreadable or non-UTF-8 files, and exceeded pack
limits fail the operation rather than silently dropping data. The UI escapes
control characters for display; the stored strings are not altered.
User-supplied collections are labelled as having unverified redistribution
rights. A local import is not permission to redistribute those files.
